    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-Research-Professor-in-Advanced-Manufacturing_REQ_0000081248-2": {
      "title": "Assistant Research Professor in Advanced Manufacturing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Harold and Inge Marcus Department of Industrial and Manufacturing Engineering at The Pennsylvania State University, University Park invites applications for a full-time Assistant Research Professor to lead and support research in advanced manufacturing. The position may involve manufacturing process development, joining and separation, repair and remanufacturing, mechanical design, materials and process characterization, sensing, and data-driven analysis for engineered products and systems. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Design and evaluate manufacturing processes, components, structures, fixtures, tooling, and/or experimental systems. Characterize process behavior, material response, defects, interfaces, and performance using appropriate experimental, sensing, or machine learning methods. Prepare peer-reviewed publications, technical reports, presentations, invention disclosures, sponsor deliverables, and research proposals. Collaborate with faculty, students, technical staff, industry partners, and government sponsors in multidisciplinary research projects. Required Qualifications Earned Ph.D. by the appointment start date in mechanical, industrial, manufacturing, materials, welding, product design, or a closely related engineering field. Demonstrated research experience in manufacturing-process development, joining or materials processing, repair/remanufacturing, mechanical or structural design, or closely related areas. Relevant capability in one or more areas such as CAD, materials characterization, process monitoring, machine learning. Strong written and oral communication skills and the ability to work effectively and collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research team. Application Materials Full curriculum vitae. Names and contact information for three professional references.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Lecturer-or-Assistant-Teaching-Professor-in-Astronomy-and-Astrophysics_REQ_0000081157-2": {
      "title": "Lecturer or Assistant Teaching Professor in Astronomy and Astrophysics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Astronomy and Astrophysics at Penn State invites applications for a full-time Lecturer or Assistant Teaching Professor position (non-tenure track) to begin by January 2027. The successful candidate will join a team that runs very large online interdomain classes in astronomy and art. They will be responsible for working on the day-to-day operations of the classes, including availability on Zoom office hours, answering student emails, grading assignments, and making course announcements. They will also be partners in efforts to improve and update the course materials, which include the University of Mars video game (written in Unity 3D), astronomy art projects, creative writing assignments, and telescope observation quests with the Slooh network. They can also participate in new video game development for other astronomy courses at Penn State, in instructional design, programming, or art design. Education and Experience The successful candidate should have a master’s degree (Lecturer) or a Ph.D. (Assistant Teaching Professor) in Astronomy, Physics, Art, or in a related field. The successful candidate should have teaching experience, a strong interest in teaching in an online format, and a student-centered, experiential teaching philosophy. They should also have experience and interest in a combination of astronomical art, video game design, video game programming, and astronomy education research. Additional Information Applications must be submitted electronically and include the following: Cover letter detailing qualifications for the position including relevant educational background as well as any related teaching experience. Curriculum vitae or resume. Statement of teaching interests. In addition, please arrange for at least three reference letters to be sent to astro-jobs@psu.edu . Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by September 30, 2026, will receive full consideration. Salary and benefits will be competitive and commensurate with the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. This position has the potential to be performed as a hybrid of remote and on-site work. For more information about our department or undergraduate program, visit https://science.psu.edu/astro .   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Postdoctoral-Scholar-in-the-Department-of-Mechanical-Engineering_REQ_0000081524-1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar in the Department of Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Mechanical Engineering at Penn State is seeking a Postdoctoral Scholar . The successful candidate will work under the supervision of Dr. Xiang Yang. Job Duties: Conduct research on turbulence modeling for compressible and high-speed flows Develop progressive flow-physics-learning and machine-learning methods Perform CFD simulations, model calibration, and model-form error analysis Benchmark turbulence models and existing compressibility corrections Verify and validate models using canonical and application-relevant flows Document results in reports, presentations, software, and publications Qualifications and Requirements:  Ph.D. or equivalent doctorate in mechanical/aerospace engineering or a related field by the appointment date Research experience in computational fluid dynamics and turbulence modeling Knowledge of compressible/high-speed flow physics and numerical methods Experience with scientific programming and high-performance computing Doctorate completed before start; appointment contingent on work authorization Interested applicants should submit a cover letter describing their interest in the position and relevant experience, a CV including a publication list, and the names and contact information of up to three references.    BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional well-being.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
