    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Research-Technology-Officer_REQ_0000080229-1": {
      "title": "Research Technology Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Penn State National Security Institute (NSI) invites applications for a non-tenure-line research faculty position to serve in a senior technical leadership role with the working title Research Technology Officer (RTO) . Appointment will be at the rank of Assistant Research Professor, Associate Research Professor, or Research Professor , depending on the successful candidate’s experience and qualifications. NSI advances interdisciplinary research, strategic partnerships, and mission-relevant innovation to address critical national security challenges. The Institute connects Penn State’s broad research capabilities with government, defense, homeland security, and industry needs, with an emphasis on technically excellent, translational, and deployable solutions. Position Overview The RTO will help shape NSI’s technical strategy and research growth by identifying emerging opportunities, building interdisciplinary teams, leading large-proposal development, and strengthening external partnerships. This is a highly collaborative role for a candidate who can operate effectively at the intersection of research strategy, technical credibility, sponsor engagement, and institutional coordination. Key Responsibilities Identify and develop strategic technical opportunities aligned with NSI priorities and sponsor needs. Lead or co-lead development of large, complex, multi-investigator and multi-institution proposals. Convene Penn State faculty and external collaborators around high-value national security challenges. Help define technical road maps for major initiatives, centers, consortia, and partnerships. Build and maintain relationships with government agencies, industry partners, laboratories, and other external stakeholders. Advise institute leadership on technical positioning, investment priorities, and capability development. Support translation of research into mission-ready, dual-use, or operationally relevant applications. Contribute to institute programs that stimulate collaboration, seed new initiatives, and strengthen proposal competitiveness. Required Qualifications Doctoral degree or equivalent terminal degree in engineering, science, technology, or a closely related field. Significant experience in technical leadership, research development, innovation strategy, or complex program development, including teams that involve federal agencies, academia, and industry. Demonstrated success working across disciplines and organizations to build strategic initiatives or externally funded efforts. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to engage effectively with academic researchers, institute leadership, and external sponsors or partners. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with DoD, DHS, DOE, NSF, intelligence-community-adjacent organizations, national laboratories, or related federal sponsors. Experience with large-scale proposal development, center formation, or research consortium building. Familiarity with technology transition, translational R&D, dual-use innovation, or mission-driven technical programs. Experience in university-based or university-connected research environments. Additional Compliance and Information-Access Requirements This position may involve access to Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), export-controlled information, or other sensitive information in support of institute activities. The successful candidate must be able to satisfy and maintain all Penn State, federal, and sponsor requirements related to accessing, handling, and protecting such information. Depending on project, sponsor, or regulatory requirements, this position may be restricted to U.S. persons (U.S. Citizens, Lawful Permanent Residents, and/or other protected individuals) as defined under applicable U.S. Export Control Regulations. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of all required background checks and any additional role-specific verifications required by Penn State, applicable law, or sponsor/contracting partner agreements. Application Materials a cover letter describing relevant experience and interest in the role; a curriculum vitae; and any additional materials requested through the final Penn State hiring process. Review of applications will begin on a rolling basis and continue until the position is filled.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES This position requires the following clearances in addition to applicable background checks: PA State Police Criminal Background Check, PA Child Abuse History Clearance Form, and Federal (FBI) Fingerprint Criminal Background Check.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Visiting-Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-in-the-Archaeology-and-History-of-the-Eastern-Mediterranean_REQ_0000080510-2": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant or Associate Professor in the Archaeology and History of the Eastern Mediterranean",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The Department of Classics and Ancient Mediterranean Studies (CAMS) and the Department of Anthropology at The Pennsylvania State University invite applications for a Visiting Assistant or Associate Professor in the area of A rchaeology and H istory of the e astern Mediterranean .  The appointment will start in January 2027 , with room for some flexibility.   This position will be filled at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor or Associate Teaching Professor . Rank will be decided based on education and experience.       Responsibilities include teaching four courses per year (two per semester), research, and some service duties. Onsite teaching is an essential function of this job.       We seek candidates who are able to teach both undergraduate and graduate courses in the material culture and histo ry of the easte rn Mediterranean . The candidate’ s scholarly expert ise may concern areas such as the Levant, Anatolia, and/or the Aegean , from ca. 3,000 BCE to ca. 300 CE . The candidate ’ s research focus may pertain to any of these regions and periods , but they should also be able to integrate material culture with textual sources . C ourses to be taught include both upper- and lower- level classes in A ncient Near Eastern and Classical Archaeology , as well as other courses on history and archaeology in the applicant’s field ; e.g., current CAMS courses, such as Lands of the Bible or Sacrifice in the Ancien t World.     The CAMS Department encompasses the entire Mediterranean and Near Eastern world in A ntiquity, and the successful candidate is expected to contribute to the dialogue across the se fields and disciplines . The ability to assist in developing the Department’s graduate program , including an M.A. in A rchaeology, and to contribute to the Department’s study abroad programs are desirable.      Candidates for the Assistant Teaching Professor rank must have a Ph.D. in Ancient Near Eastern Studies, Mediterranean or Near Eastern Archaeology, Ancient History, Anthropology with specialization in the eastern Mediterranean or Levant, Classics, or a closely related field , i n hand by the start date. Candidates should also provide a record of scholarly p ublication and productivity, as well as evidence of undergraduate-level teaching experience.      Candidates for the Associate Teaching Professor rank must have all aforementioned requirements along with substantial undergraduate - and/or graduate-level teaching experience.      The College of the Liberal Arts is committed to offering professional growth and promotional opportunities for non-tenure-line faculty appointments.  Information on faculty ranks and progression can be found at  https://policy.psu.edu/policies/ac21       To be considered for this position, applications must be submitted online at Penn State's Job Posting Board , and should upload the following application materials: a letter of interest, CV or resume, a sample of scholarly writing, and evidence of teaching excellence. Candidates should also arrange to have three letters of recommendation submitted to Lynn Carey, Administrative Assistant, at lmc5897@psu.edu .     Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to the Head of the Department of Classics and Ancient Mediterranean Studies, Prof. Tawny Holm, at tholm@psu.edu .     Visit our website at https://cams.la.psu.edu/ for more details on our Department.     BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Huck-Institutes-of-the-Life-Sciences-NSF-NCEMS-Researcher_REQ_0000080649-2": {
      "title": "Huck Institutes of the Life Sciences NSF NCEMS Researcher",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS POSITION DESCRIPTION The Huck Institutes of The Life Sciences ( The Huck ) and the U.S. National Science Foundation National Synthesis Center for Emergence in the Molecular and Cellular Sciences ( NCEMS ) seek to hire a Researcher to support and advance NCEMS’s mission of catalyzing and conducting community-scale synthesis in the molecular and cellular sciences through research and externally facing activities. The successful candidate will contribute to a dynamic and collaborative research environment and will work closely with internal and external faculty, staff, students, and partners. This position is intended to support an individual in the early stages of a research career who will contribute to ongoing research efforts while continuing to build expertise in computational and data-intensive synthesis science. The role is primarily research-focused and emphasizes interdisciplinary collaboration, reproducible analytical approaches, and scholarly output. RESPONSIBILITIES Advance the NCEMS mission through participation in community-scale synthesis research in the molecular and cellular sciences Contribute to research activities involving computational biology, bioinformatics, biological data analysis, and related quantitative approaches Analyze and interpret complex molecular and cellular datasets Collaborate with interdisciplinary teams across NCEMS and with external research partners Contribute to the preparation of technical reports, manuscripts, presentations, and other research outputs Support the development and application of reproducible and open-science-oriented research workflows, tools, and resources Participate in scientific meetings, project discussions, and other research activities that contribute to the progress of NCEMS initiatives Assist with mentoring graduate and undergraduate students, as appropriate, in support of research activities MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in Computational Biology, Bioinformatics, Biosciences, Plant Sciences, Computer Science, Statistics, or a related field Demonstrated experience in computational biology, bioinformatics, AI-driven biological data analysis, and scalable open-science research infrastructure and training Strong written and verbal communication skills Demonstrated ability to contribute to research products such as analyses, manuscripts, technical reports, presentations, or related scholarly outputs PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience working with large-scale biological datasets Experience with reproducible computational workflows and open-science research practices Experience contributing to externally funded research projects Experience working collaboratively across disciplines and with research teams Record of publications, manuscripts in preparation, technical reports, or other scholarly contributions Interest in community-scale synthesis research in the molecular and cellular sciences APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS Applicants must submit: A cover letter describing relevant experience and interests A current curriculum vitae (CV) Contact information for three professional references Applications must be submitted electronically through Penn State’s employment system.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-of-Law---Penn-State-Dickinson-Law--University-Park-_REQ_0000080655-1": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Law - Penn State Dickinson Law (University Park)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants .   POSITION SPECIFICS Penn State Dickinson Law invites applications from both entry-level and junior lateral candidates for a tenure-track faculty position (Assistant or Associate Professor of Law), with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027, at our University Park, Pennsylvania location. We are seeking candidates to annually teach Contracts and Sales alongside two courses of their scholarly interest and our institutional need .  Candidates may bring a wide range of qualifications, including relevant teaching or practice experience, judicial clerkships at any level, interdisciplinary scholarly work, or post-J.D. studies, degrees, or certificates. The successful candidate will be expected to: Produce high-quality scholarly research in the field of law, Teach law courses and demonstrate excellence in the classroom, Supervise and mentor student research assistants, and Provide service to the law school, university, and broader professional community. A demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence, impactful scholarship, and student mentorship is essential. About Dickinson Law: Founded in 1834, Penn State Dickinson Law is the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania’s first law school and one of the oldest in the nation. Fully accredited by the ABA and a member of the AALS since 1912, Dickinson Law’s mission is to educate and train lawyers equipped to excel in an evolving legal profession. The Law School is guided by core values of teaching, scholarship, service, and community, which define our mission and culture. As part of The Pennsylvania State University, Penn State Dickinson Law values belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission. Penn State’s Values may be found here . The position is based in University Park, PA. The University prioritizes regular on-site presence to support full engagement in the campus community. Full-time, tenured or tenure-track faculty are expected to teach in-person and work on-site. Questions about work arrangements should be directed to the hiring manager during the interview process.            All candidate materials must be submitted via the Penn State Career website. Interested candidates should upload a cover letter and a resume or CV. A candidate’s application materials are expected to provide clear evidence supporting Penn State values and accessibility throughout their teaching, research, and/or service.             Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Candidates should provide the names, titles, and contact information (telephone, email, and mailing address) of three (3) professional references. Candidates who advance in the search will be notified to confirm that their references may be contacted. Questions may be sent to the Appointments Committee Chair through Melissa Walters at mbw5955@psu.edu. Applications received by September 18, 2026, will receive full consideration; however, the search will continue until the positions are filled.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Multiple-Open-Rank-Professor-Tenure-Track-Positions-in-Organizational-Behavior--Organizational-Theory--or-Strategy_REQ_0000080154-1": {
      "title": "Multiple Open-Rank Professor Tenure-Track Positions in Organizational Behavior, Organizational Theory, or Strategy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants .   POSITION SPECIFICS The Management and Organization (M&O) Department in the Smeal College of Business at The Pennsylvania State University (University Park, PA) has two full-time tenure-track professor positions in the areas of Organizational Behavior (OB), Organizational Theory (OT), or Strategy. We seek to fill these positions at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor . The desired start date for the position is Fall 2027. Those who are in the final stages of completing a PhD program will be considered for appointments as an Assistant Professor. For consideration for Associate or Full Professor level positions, applicants must have a proven track record in conducting high-quality scholarly research and demonstrated teaching competence at a high level. Candidates for all ranks must have a PhD in Management or a related field by the appointment start date. Candidates at the Associate or Full Professor rank must also have demonstrated both a sufficient number of publications in high-quality journals and sufficient impact of that work on the field. Job Requirement : The preferred candidate will have publications in premier journals, a research program with high-impact or such potential underway and is able to connect with a wide array of doctoral students and faculty in our department. Faculty members in the M&O department are expected to pursue an active research program, perform undergraduate and/or graduate teaching, supervise graduate students, and engage in professional service. Onsite teaching is an essential function of the job. Candidates for the position can apply by uploading a letter of interest, CV, and three research papers. Candidates should also have three reference letters sent directly to mandosmeal@psu.edu . System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5 document limitations. Any questions about the position can be sent to Amanda Brown, M&O Support Coordinator, at the same email. Review of applications for the position will begin on September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. The Department of Management and Organization is consistently ranked in the top-20 management departments for its research productivity and values high-level theoretical and empirical ability, collegiality and collaboration among its members, and the ability to teach management and organizational concepts effectively to multiple audiences. Our department offers two undergraduate majors (Corporate Innovation and Entrepreneurship; Management), two online masters programs (Corporate Innovation and Entrepreneurship; Strategic Management and Executive Leadership), a PhD program, courses in Smeal’s full-time rMBA and DBA programs, courses in Smeal’s part-time hMBA and OBMA, and operates the Farrell Center for Corporate Innovation and Entrepreneurship (which includes the Garber Venture Capital Fund). Our tenure-line faculty are Heejung Byun, Carolyn Dang, Raghu Garud, Don Hambrick, Stephen Humphrey, Trevor Israelsen, Jon Jachimowicz, Margaret Luciano, Vilmos Misangyi, Semin Park, Tessa Recendes, Kira Schabram, Paul Shrivastava, Linda Treviño, Wenpin Tsai, Dani Yin, and Rui Zhong. Our nontenure-line clinical faculty are Shawn Clark, Sean Doherty, Jeanette Miller, Lisa O’Hara, Özge Pala, Federica Pinelli, and Angela Schwartz. Our nontenure-line full-time teaching faculty are Cameron Conaway, Neil Fogarty, Ron Johnson, James Jones, Dave Lenze, Travis Lesser, and Brad Leve. For more information on our department please visit https://www.smeal.psu.edu/management . The M&O Department is part of the Smeal College of Business, which depends on more than 360 faculty and staff to enact and support its strategic priorities of integrity, diversity, and sustainability and to serve the needs of more than 9,000 students. Media outlets and independent observers regularly rank Smeal among the best business schools in the world. Please visit http://www.smeal.psu.edu/ for additional information. The Smeal College of Business is located at the Pennsylvania State University’s main campus (University Park) in the heart of State College, Pennsylvania. Our community features the charms of a small town with the opportunities typically only found in larger cities, with State College routinely ranked among the top 10 best college towns in the United States ( https://www.collegetransitions.com/blog/best-college-towns-in-america/ ).   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
    },
    "https://psu.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Penn-State-University-Park/Smeal-Marketing-Dept-open-rank-tenure-track-position_REQ_0000080142": {
      "title": "Smeal Marketing Dept. open rank tenure track position",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants .   POSITION SPECIFICS The Marketing Department in the Smeal College of Business, Penn State University (University Park, PA) seeks to fill multiple tenure-track faculty positions (open rank). We seek to fill these positions at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor . The desired start date for the positions is Fall 2027. T hose who are in the final stages of completing a PhD program will be considered for appointments as an Assistant Professor. For consideration for Associate or Full Professor level positions, applicants must have a proven track record in conducting high-quality scholarly research and demonstrated teaching competence at a high level. Experienced applicants who wish to be considered at the Associate or Full level should have the same qualifications as the Assistant Professor, but should also have demonstrated both a sufficient number of publications in high-quality journals and sufficient impact of that work on the field. Candidates for all ranks must have a PhD in Marketing or a related field by the appointment start date. Although research focus is open, preference will be given to those in Quantitative Modeling and/or Marketing Management and Strategy . Penn State faculty members are expected to pursue an active research program, perform undergraduate and graduate teaching, supervise graduate students, and engage in service activities. Salary and benefits will be competitive and commensurate with the background and experience of the chosen candidate. Applications should be submitted online via the PSU site. Applicants should upload a CV and cover letter, and may also provide optional supporting documents (e.g., letters of recommendation, working or published research papers, research and teaching statements, course evaluations). System limitations allow for a total of 5 documents (5mb per document) as part of your application. Please combine materials to meet the 5-document limit. If you have any questions regarding the positions, please contact Meg Meloy, Department Chair ( mgm16@psu.edu ). For questions about the application process and Workday portal, please contact Hollie Meyer ( hlm5317@psu.edu ). Please include “Marketing Tenure Track Position 2027” in the subject line of any email correspondence. More information about the Department and the Smeal College of Business is available at https://www.smeal.psu.edu/marketing .   Review of applications will begin late August and continue until the position is filled.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provides a competitive benefits package for full-time employees designed to support both personal and professional wellbeing. In addition to comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage, employees enjoy robust retirement plans. One of the standout benefits is the generous 75% tuition discount, available to employees as well as eligible spouses and children.   For more detailed information, please visit our  Benefits Page. (Note: For Postdoctoral benefits, please see our Postdoctoral Benefits page.)   CAMPUS SECURITY CRIME STATISTICS Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act and the Pennsylvania Act of 1988, Penn State publishes a combined Annual Security and Annual Fire Safety Report (ASR). The ASR includes crime statistics and institutional policies concerning campus security, such as those concerning alcohol and drug use, crime prevention, the reporting of crimes, sexual assault, and other matters. The ASR is available for review here .   EEO IS THE LAW Penn State is an equal opportunity employer and is committed to providing employment opportunities to all qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability or protected veteran status. If you are unable to use our online application process due to an impairment or disability, please contact 814-865-1473.   Penn State is committed to and accountable for advancing equity, respect, and belonging. We embrace individual uniqueness, as well as a culture of belonging that supports equity initiatives, leverages the educational and institutional benefits of inclusion in society, and provides opportunities for engagement intended to help all members of the community thrive. We value belonging as a core strength and an essential element of the university’s teaching, research, and service mission.   Federal Contractors Labor Law Poster PA State Labor Law Poster Penn State Policies Copyright Information Hotlines"
