      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Chemistry",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: CURRENT PENN STATE EMPLOYEE (faculty, staff, technical service, or student), please login to Workday to complete the internal application process . Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. CURRENT PENN STATE STUDENT (not employed previously at the university) and seeking employment with Penn State, please login to Workday to complete the student application process. Please do not apply here, apply internally through Workday. If you are NOT a current employee or student, please click “Apply” and complete the application process for external applicants .   Approval of remote and hybrid work is not guaranteed regardless of work location. For additional information on remote work at Penn State, see  Notice to Out of State Applicants . This is a term position; length of the term will be discussed during the interview process. Continuation past the term length discussed will be based on university need, performance, and/or availability of funding.   POSITION SPECIFICS The laboratory of Professor Yi Liu in the Department of Chemistry at The Pennsylvania State University is seeking highly motivated postdoctoral researcher to work in the areas of biocatalysis and synthetic chemistry. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in chemistry. Candidates with expertise in organic synthesis, enzyme studies, or related areas are especially encouraged to apply. Interested candidates should submit their application electronically, including a CV and research summary. After an initial review, selected candidates will be contacted by email and asked to arrange for letters of recommendation. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.   BACKGROUND CHECKS/CLEARANCES Employment with the University will require successful completion of background check(s) in accordance with University policies.       BENEFITS Penn State provide